{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And if.</b> He took a terse path, like שלש סאים (Genesis 18:6), for the correct reading is 'these three.' Many thought that 'these three' are her food, her clothing, and her conjugal rights, but this is impossible, for after it says כמשפט הבנות יעשה לה (Exodus 21:9), and the obligation of daughters is these three, and there is no need to mention this. Furthermore, because regarding the beautiful woman, who is a non-Israelite, it is written about her: ומכור לא תמכרנה בכסף (Deuteronomy 21:14) — all the more so this one. Rather, the correct reading is 'and if one of these three' — namely, if he does not designate her, or if his son is not designated for her, and if she is not redeemed — she goes out free, she being in her own jurisdiction. And like it: אם יגע טמא נפש בכל אלה היטמא (Haggai 2:13), meaning in one of these; and many similar cases. The Gaon [Saadia] asked: what reason is there to say 'no money' after it already says ויצאה חנם? And he answered that if she fell ill in his house and he spent on her for medical treatment, she does not repay him anything. In my opinion this is unnecessary, for it is an added clarification, in the manner of כי מת אתה ולא תחיה (2 Kings 20:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:50.405185081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}